    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103268" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετᾰγών</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όντος</span>,
			ὁ, 
			Ep.
		 redupl. part.
		aor. 2, with no pres. in use, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥῖψε ποδὸς τεταγών</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>having seized</i> him
			<i>by</i> the foot, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.591
			</span></i>; also simply, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥίπτασκον τεταγών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					15.23
				</span></i>
			. (Cf. Lat. <i>tango, tetigi.</i>)</div>
